→ list: jsn flows list — Back to all flows</pre></div>
            </details>
        </div>

        <section class="why" style="margin: 3rem 0; text-align: center;">
            <h2 style="color: var(--accent); font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-family: 'SF Mono', Monaco, monospace;">Why jsn exists</h2>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.8;">
                When I started this in March 2026, the ServiceNow SDK couldn't read a record from a live instance. It could only build. So I built what I wanted: a CLI that works with your data across scopes.
            </p>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); max-width: 640px; margin: 0.75rem auto 0; line-height: 1.8;">
                now-sdk added live queries in June 2026. Good for them. But reading records was never the whole point.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="features">
            <h2 style="color: var(--accent); font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-family: 'SF Mono', Monaco, monospace; text-align: center; grid-column: 1 / -1;">What it does that plain REST doesn't</h2>

            <div class="feature">
                <h3>Context, not just REST</h3>
                <p>Load a catalog item and get its variables. Load a flow and get its subflows. Related records, resolved. Plain REST doesn't do that.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="feature">
                <h3>Agent-Native</h3>
                <p>JSON output and breadcrumbs for agents. Works with Hermes, Claude, Codex, Cursor, OpenCode, Copilot. The skill is a markdown file, no MCP server to stand up. CLIs run on a fraction of the context MCP servers eat (<a href="https://layered.dev/mcp-tool-schema-bloat-the-hidden-token-tax-and-how-to-fix-it/" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent);">why</a>), and even the protocol's own repo admits the bloat problem (<a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/discussions/2036" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent);">discussion #2036</a>).</p>
                <div class="code-block">
                    <span class="cmd">jsn incidents list --json</span> <span class="comment"># Structured output</span><br>
                    <span class="cmd">jsn skill install</span> <span class="comment"># Expert knowledge for your agent</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="feature">
                <h3>The docs, local</h3>
                <p>All ~50,000 ServiceNow docs, indexed, searchable instantly, offline. Ask the difference between Flow Designer and Playbooks and get an answer from the docs, not a guess.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="feature">
                <h3>Auth that just works</h3>
                <p>OAuth handled. The part raw AI plus REST keeps tripping on.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="feature">
                <h3>Safe by default</h3>
                <p>Read-only by default. Deletes are blocked unless you pass --force. You can even mark a profile read-only and mutations are blocked entirely.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="feature">
                <h3>Small by design</h3>
                <p>They declare 3 dependencies. You end up with 628 packages and 353 MB. We declare 6. You end up with 90 and 41 MB. None of ours are abandoned. Three of theirs are.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section style="text-align: center; padding: 2rem 0;">
            <p style="color: var(--muted);">
                Install: <code style="color: var(--accent);">npm install -g @jacebenson/jsn</code> · Auth: <code style="color: var(--accent);">jsn setup</code> · Agents: <code style="color: var(--accent);">jsn skill install</code>
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">
                <a href="https://github.com/jacebenson/jsn/blob/nodejs/skills/servicenow/SKILL.md" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;">Full setup guide &amp; skill docs →</a>
            </p>
        </section>

        <section style="text-align: center; padding: 2rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 3rem;">
            <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem;">Open source, MIT. Runs locally. No analytics, nothing phones home. Credentials stay in your config.</p>
        </section>

        <footer class="footer">
            <a href="https://github.com/jacebenson/jsn" class="github-link">github.com/jacebenson/jsn</a>
            <p>Open source • MIT License</p>
        </footer>
    </div>

    <script>
        // Copy npm install command
        function copyNpmInstall() {
            const code = 'npm install -g @jacebenson/jsn';
            navigator.clipboard.writeText(code).then(() => {
                const btn = event.target;
                btn.textContent = 'Copied!';
                setTimeout(() => btn.textContent = 'Copy', 2000);
            }).catch(() => {
                // Fallback for browsers that don't support clipboard API
                const textarea = document.createElement('textarea');
                textarea.value = code;
                document.body.appendChild(textarea);
                textarea.select();
                document.execCommand('copy');
                document.body.removeChild(textarea);
                const btn = event.target;
                btn.textContent = 'Copied!';
                setTimeout(() => btn.textContent = 'Copy', 2000);
            });
        }

        // Copy a demo command
        function copyDemo(btn, cmd) {
            navigator.clipboard.writeText(cmd).then(() => {
                btn.textContent = 'Copied!';
                setTimeout(() => btn.textContent = 'Copy', 2000);
            }).catch(() => {
                const textarea = document.createElement('textarea');
                textarea.value = cmd;
                document.body.appendChild(textarea);
                textarea.select();
                document.execCommand('copy');
                document.body.removeChild(textarea);
                btn.textContent = 'Copied!';
                setTimeout(() => btn.textContent = 'Copy', 2000);
            });
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>